# A test module is a child module (claude/modules-style-pass.md, Jimmy's ruling of 5
# November): `test mod Tests` declares `tests.prism`, the module `Tests` beside the root's
# other children, read only by `prism test` and `prism check`. It reaches its parent by
# `use`, as any child does: the root's test module by `use App.*` (the root of a program
# tree, named by its file), `Counter.Tests` by `use Counter.*`. A test module may name
# another test module's helpers (`Counter.Tests.Stepped`).
# Written by Claude on the claude-self-hosting branch; subject to change.
emit Ui.*
mod Counter
test mod Tests
use Ui
use Counter.*

Caption: fn Nat -> Text
fn Caption n = "{Step n} steps"

@main: @unit
@main:
    !next <- Ui.Button(label=$"Next")                       # 0
    $n <- 0 then $n + 1 on !next
    Ui.Label(text=(Caption $n))                            # 1
